    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1259">

                <pb facs="0873" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/415.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s August 22, regarding payment of mining taxes in Mexico Department’s
                    objection is sustained, exception being made of cases in which payments were
                    made to Huerta officials when they could have been made to Constitutionalist
                    authorities in territory occupied by the Constitutionalists. For instance taxes
                    on Sonora properties paid to Huerta authorities in Mexico City would not be
                    considered valid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
